\title{svysem: Design-Based Structural Equation Models for Complex Surveys}
\description{
Design-based estimation of structural equation models fitted with 'lavaan' for data stored in a 'survey' design. Sampling weights, clustering and stratification enter the variance as in 'Mplus' TYPE=COMPLEX. The design-based covariance of the sample moments is passed to 'lavaan', which returns robust standard errors and a scaled test (Oberski (2014) \doi{10.18637/jss.v057.i01}). Each completed data set of a multiple imputation is fitted separately and the estimates are pooled with Rubin's rules, using the design degrees of freedom as the complete-data degrees of freedom (Rubin (1987) \doi{10.1002/9780470316696}; Barnard and Rubin (1999) \doi{10.1093/biomet/86.4.948}).
}
